  const optGuide=document.createElement('details');optGuide.className='foot';optGuide.innerHTML='<summary><strong>Design-variable bounds used by the search</strong></summary><table class="metrics"><tr><th>Variable</th><th>User input / fixed condition</th><th>Role in the routing search</th></tr><tr><td>Plan area A</td><td>60–600 m²; 20 m² increment</td><td>Defines the constant-area storage geometry. It is searched in every candidate plan.</td></tr><tr><td>Weir width b</td><td>Enter a minimum and maximum (default 0.05–1.00 m). Crest elevation P and coefficient Cw remain fixed.</td><td>Changes the weir discharge capacity above its crest.</td></tr><tr><td>Orifice area Ao</td><td>Enter a minimum and maximum (default 0.005–0.050 m²). Invert elevation and Cd remain fixed.</td><td>Changes the submerged-orifice capacity above its invert.</td></tr><tr><td>Riser diameter D</td><td>Enter a minimum and maximum (default 0.15–0.60 m). Riser crest/invert and Cr/Cd remain fixed.</td><td>Changes both the riser inlet and shaft capacity; the smaller controls.</td></tr></table><p>Every selected outlet-size variable is tested at five equally spaced values, including its declared minimum and maximum. Select no more than two size variables; an unselected size remains fixed at its Outlet-module value. The recommended sizes and their engineering meaning are reported on the right after routing every candidate.</p>';
